Break Room is a web page a group of people open together to see who is
around and play short games — trivia first, more to follow — beside a voice
or video call they already have open. It was conceived, designed and written
by Charles Adams as an independent personal project:

  * Built on personally owned hardware, using a personal Anthropic (Claude)
    subscription paid for by the author.
  * Developed in the author's personal GitHub account (eagleadams86).
  * No employer equipment, funding, source code or libraries were used.
  * No employer confidential or proprietary information is present in this
    repository or in the application. There is nothing to be present: a room
    holds nicknames people choose for the evening, the answers they give to
    invented quiz questions, and a running score, and all of it is deleted
    within a day. Nothing from any work system is asked for or stored.

The quiz questions embedded in the page were written for this project and
are general knowledge; none is drawn from any employer's material.

